NAME
       hostname - show or set the system host name

SYNOPSIS
       hostname [-s] [NAME]

DESCRIPTION
       Without NAME, print the host name of the current UTS namespace.
       With NAME, set it (root only). The change affects only the running
       UTS namespace of the caller and is not written to /etc/hostname.

OPTIONS
       -s
           short name, cut at the first dot

EXAMPLES
       hostname
       sudo hostname box

SEE ALSO
       uname(1), unshare(1), nsenter(1)
